{
  "_comment": [
    "Canary suite: category queries with hand-picked canonical answers.",
    "",
    "Unlike qrels.json (LLM-judged, pooled), these labels are human-curated",
    "from cross-referenced awesome-list / ecosystem consensus, so the canary",
    "recall metric is immune to judge drift and gives a true recall",
    "denominator. Every full_name was verified present in the corpus on the",
    "date below (several use post-rename owners, e.g. react/react and",
    "rwf2/Rocket — the corpus stores current GitHub names).",
    "",
    "The metric: canary recall@10 = |top-10 ∩ expected| / |expected|,",
    "averaged over queries. It answers 'when a stranger types a category,",
    "do the repos everyone would name actually show up?'",
    "",
    "Expected lists are deliberately short (1-5): only repos that ecosystem",
    "consensus would definitely name, not everything plausibly relevant.",
    "Finding OTHER good repos is not penalised by this metric (that is what",
    "the judged nDCG measures); missing THESE is.",
    "",
    "Frozen after the hand-review pass. Append-only afterwards; never relabel to",
    "make a run look better."
  ],
